==Battleground==
*1 [[Mr. Mer]] spawns after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
*1 [[Cala Maria]] spawns after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.
*1 [[Spacefish Jones]] spawns as the boss after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The stage can be quickly cleaned up by luring Mr. Mer out and destroying him with high-damage units such as [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]], [[Dom Cat (Special Cat)|Dark Lazer]], etc. while also making use of [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] and [[Mightycat (Rare Cat)|Supercat]] to stop the [[Wave Attack#Mini-Wave|Mini-Wave]] damage. Once he is dead, nothing will stop you from clearing out the remaining peons. [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]] can be used to pilfer extra money before and after Mr. Mer dies. Use four or more meatshields for Cala Maria.

[[Ancient Egg: N005 (Special Cat)|Hitman Cat]], if it has been acquired at this point in the game, can completely destroy the stage with his Wave Immunity and Massive Damage against Traitless.

==Trivia==
*This stage's name refers to the famous [[wikipedia:Merlion|Merlion]] statues of Singapore, which served as the basis for [[Mr. Mer]]'s design.
*Fish-Legged Beauty's Japanese, Tempting Fish-Legged Mermaid, may also be a reference to the song "HOT LIMIT" by [[wikipedia:Takanori Nishikawa|T.M. Revolution]]; one of the lyrics can be translated as "With all those bare-legged mermaids around tempting me..."

